each stamping `:dao.star/lineage` on its facts, renewals and release, and the judge's resolver reads that key; until ShiBi, any writer of that medium can renew, the same exposure the exchange lease has. The driver observes its grant before consuming or projecting, renews at under half the duration from its own control flow, on each consumed input and on its tick while it holds an open subscription, and **stops at its bound**: past it, it consumes nothing and projects nothing, and an input arriving then is handed to the root program as begin. So a connected session is retained for as long as it stays connected, by design, bounded only by the cap; a disconnected one lapses after the idle allowance. The lease ends with the lineage: released by the driver on halt, lapsed by the judge on silence. Reclaim retires the runnable resource, the current parked record; the `:lapsed` record on the lease medium is the judge's own and is what ends the lineage for the router. History, successor facts and lease records are kept (`dao.lease.md`: a reclaim frees the resource, never the record). The subject is distinct from Mode 2's custody subject `{:yin.k/occurrence O}` on the arbitration medium. Leases are process-scoped until the composition settles the three durable duties `dao.lease.md` names.\\ndocs/design/dao.agent.harness.md:204:that the seat releases the claim (`:claim/status :released`) and the\\ndocs/design/dao.agent.harness.md:246:|             |               | :claim/status :released              |\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:76:latest release on 2026-09-16 against\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:80:preserves released tag meanings and older-output readability, but does not\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:81:promise identical encoding bytes across releases (verified against that\\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:1307:7. **Explicit Over Implicit** — No hidden expiration, no automatic cleanup, no magic. Application logic drives coordination policy.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn