|                  |\\n2214\\t|                     | supported builtin declares its      |                  |\\n2215\\t|                     | by-reference positions; the notice  |                  |\\n2216\\t|                     | is emitted; prefer-ref builtins are |                  |\\n2217\\t|                     | refused                             |                  |\\n2218\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\n2219\\t| C7 return by        | Engine: `function &f()`, `&__get`,  | unsupported; a   |\\n2220\\t| reference           | `&offsetGet`. Here: refused         | slice after P9   |\\n2221\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\n2222\\t| C8 generator        | Engine: destroying a suspended      | restricted; P4-c |\\n2223\\t| destruction         | generator runs its pending          |                  |\\n2224\\t|                     | `finally` blocks and releases its   |                  |\\n2225\\t|                     | frame. Here: its CVs are released   |                  |\\n2226\\t|                     | (rows 16, 39) but pending `finally` |                  |\\n2227\\t|                     | blocks do not run                   |                  |\\n2228\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\n2229\\t| C9                  | Engine: `Attempt to destruct        | restricted; none |\\n2230\\t| pending-exception   | pending exception`. Here: an        | planned          |\\n2231\\t| destruct fatal      | `Error`-class halt with pinned      |                  |\\n2232\\t|                     | text, not a process fatal           |                  |\\n2233\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\n2234\\t| C10 property hooks, | Engine: PHP 8.4. Here: not parsed   | unsupported; a   |\\n2235\\t| asymmetric          | (8.3 pinned)                        | grammar and      |\\n2236\\t| visibility          |                                     | version bump     |\\n2237\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\n2238\\t| C11 dynamic-scope   | Engine: `extract(EXTR_REFS)`,       | unsupported      |\\n2239\\t| references          | `compact` of references, `$$name =& | until P9         |\\n2240\\t|                     | ...`, `get_defined_vars`. Here: the |                  |\\n2241\\t|                     | symbol table holds markers like any |                  |\\n2242\\t|                     | location; `EXTR_REFS` and `$$x =&`  |                  |\\n2243\\t|                     | are refused                         |                  |\\n2244\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\n2245\\t| C12 nested          | Engine: `[[&$a]] = ...` and keyed   | restricted; P9   |\\n2246\\t| destructuring by    | nested forms. Here: one level (row  |                  |\\n2247\\t| reference           | 47); deeper refused                 |                  |\\n2248\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\n2249\\t| C13 `$GLOBALS`      | Engine: `$GLOBALS` is a read-only   | restricted; P9   |\"}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_wD7K86UI30Hy9KhZtijUiHyr\",\"content\":\"320\\t\\n321\\t- `Throwable` with the `Exception` and `Error` hierarchies (`TypeError`,\\n322\\t  `ValueError`, `ArgumentCountError`, `ArithmeticError`,\\n323\\t  `DivisionByZeroError`, `UnhandledMatchError`, `JsonException`, the SPL\\n324\\t  exceptions); `try`/`catch` (multi-type `|`, optional variable)/`finally`;\\n325\\t  `throw` as an expression (8.0).\\n326\\t- **Warnings, notices and deprecations are not exceptions**: they are\\n327\\t  `:php.diag/warning` records appended to a guest-diagnostics stream the\\n328\\t  composition supplies (deterministic, since they derive from program state;\\n329\\t  owner decision B8.4), observable by `set_error_handler`, a guest callable in\\n330\\t  a cell invoked at the emission point by prelude code. `ErrorException`\\n331\\t  conversion is then user code.\\n332\\t- **`@`** lowers the expression's diagnostics with `error_reporting()`\\n333\\t  temporarily reduced to the PHP 8 mask (`E_ERROR | E_PARSE | E_CORE_ERROR |\\n334\\t  E_COMPILE_ERROR | E_USER_ERROR | E_RECOVERABLE_ERROR`). A handler installed\\n335\\t  by `set_error_handler` is **still invoked** and observes the reduced value;\\n336\\t  only the default output is silenced.\\n337\\t- `E_ERROR` fatals (undefined class, abstract instantiation) are `Error`\\n338\\t  throws. The uncaught-exception text is pinned to PHP's `PHP Fatal error:\\n339\\t  Uncaught ...` format without the file path.\\n340\\t\\n341\\t### 3.10 Generators and iteration protocols\\n342\\t\\n343\\t`yield`, `yield k => v`, `send`, `throw`, `getReturn` and `yield from` map\\n344\\tonto the landed C2 core (switch, yield-raw, exit, flag cells, a per-generator\\n345\\thandler stack); `Generator` implements `Iterator`. `foreach` drives arrays and\\n346\\t`Iterator`/`IteratorAggregate` objects; `ArrayAccess` and `Countable` are\\n347\\tsupported. Destroying a suspended generator releases its CVs but does not run\\n348\\tits pending `finally` blocks (corner C8, closed by P4-c).\\n349\\t\\n350\\t### 3.11 Mixed HTML mode\\n351\\t\\n352\\t`inlineHtml` tokens lower to `php/echo` of the literal text in source order\\n353\\tbetween code blocks. `?>` swallows one following newline (the lexer's rule,\\n354\\tpreserved through the span); the first `<?php` has no output before it unless\\n355\\tthere is text. Output order is statement order: exit criterion 1 is a direct\\n356\\tfixture.\\n357\\t\\n358\\t### 3.12 eval\\n359\\t\\n360\\t`eval` is a new compilation request (`yang.antlr.md` 8.6) sharing the caller's\\n361\\tscope, so it forces the dynamic-scope profile on its function. It is refused\\n362\\twith `:yang.php/unsupported :eval` until its slice (P9).\\n363\\t\\n364\\t## 4. The reference, array and object lifecycle\\n365\\t\\n366\\tPHP's observable aliasing (references, copy-on-write separation that unwraps\\n367\\tunshared references, destructor timing) is defined by the Zend engine's\\n368\\toperations, so this model is derived from them, not from an abstraction. Each\\n369\\trow names the Zend handler it maps to; each row is normative and is confirmed\\n370\\tagainst the pinned PHP CLI before the slice that claims it lands (the blocking\\n371\\trule, section 17.3).\\n372\\t\\n373\\t### 4.1 What the engine does\\n374\\t\\n375\\t- A **zval** is a typed slot in a CV, a hashtable bucket, a property table or\\n376\\t  a temporary. Refcounted kinds carry a header: strings, arrays\\n377\\t  (`zend_array`), objects, resources and references (`zend_reference\\n378\\t  {refcount, val}`).\\n379\\t- **Copying a zval** (`$b = $a`, `SEND_VAR`, `RETURN`, the `FE_RESET_R`\\n380\\t  temporary, array-literal elements) copies the slot and `GC_ADDREF`s the\\n381\\t  pointee: for an array, the **hashtable**, never its elements. Literal arrays\\n382\\t  are immutable and uncounted; the first write duplicates.\\n383\\t- **Writing into an array** goes through a write-address fetch (`FETCH_DIM_W`,\\n384\\t  `FETCH_OBJ_W`, `FETCH_DIM_RW`): the container is separated\\n385\\t  (`SEPARATE_ARRAY`, `zend_array_dup`) when its refcount is above 1, a missing\\n386\\t  key is auto-vivified, and the element's address is returned. `$a[k] = v`,\\n387\\t  `$r =& $a[k]`, a by-reference `f($a[k])`, `foreach ($a as &$v)` and `$a[] =\\n388\\t  v` all use this path, separating each level as reached.\\n389\\t- **`zend_array_dup`** copies buckets; a reference with refcount 1 whose value\\n390\\t  is not the array being duplicated is **unwrapped** in the copy (the copy\\n391\\t  holds the value, `ADDREF`ed); any other refcounted element is `ADDREF`ed;\\n392\\t  the source is unchanged; registered iterator positions are duplicated onto\\n393\\t  the copy.\\n394\\t- **`ASSIGN`** dereferences a reference destination, acquires the new value,\\n395\\t  stores it, then destroys the old one. **`ASSIGN_REF`** fetches the source\\n396\\t  for write, does nothing when source and destination are the same zval, wraps\\n397\\t  a non-reference source in place, `ADDREF`s the reference, stores it, then\\n398\\t  destroys the old destination content: acquisition precedes release.\\n399\\t- **`UNSET_CV`** `DELREF`s whatever the CV holds; unset fetches separate but\\n400\\t  never vivify. **Function exit** releases every CV, on normal return and on\\n401\\t  unwinding.\\n402\\t- **Objects** are handles: property writes do not separate; the object is\\n403\\t  refcounted and finalized at zero; cycles are reclaimed later by the cycle\\n404\\t  collector.\\n405\\t\\n406\\t### 4.2 The substrate mapping\\n407\\t\\n408\\tEvery Zend refcounted kind whose count is **observable** becomes a heap cell\\n409\\twith an explicit `:rc`; kinds whose count is unobservable stay plain values.\\n410\\t\\n411\\t+-------------------------+-------------------------+--------------------------+\\n412\\t| Zend kind               | Substrate               | Why                      |\\n413\\t+=========================+=========================+==========================+\\n414\\t| string                  | plain value             | immutable semantics;     |\\n415\\t|                         |                         | separation never         |\\n416\\t|                         |                         | observable               |\\n417\\t+-------------------------+-------------------------+--------------------------+\\n418\\t| array transitively      | plain persistent        | duplicating such a table |\\n419\\t| holding no reference,   | ordered map, stored     | is observable only       |\\n420\\t| instance handle or      | directly in its holder  | through unwrapping, and  |\\n421\\t| object handle           |                         | there is nothing inside  |\\n422\\t|                         |                         | to unwrap or release;    |\\n423\\t|                         |                         | copy-on-write is free    |\\n424\\t+-------------------------+-------------------------+--------------------------+\\n425\\t| any other array         | instance cell           | its duplication and      |\\n426\\t|                         | `{:php/type :arr :rc n  | destruction perform      |\\n427\\t|                         | :value <ordered map>    | observable `ADDREF`,     |\\n428\\t|                         | :deps #{keys}           | `DELREF` and unwrapping  |\\n429\\t|                         | :iterators #{it} :ptr   | on elements              |\\n430\\t|                         | i}`, held through       |                          |\\n431\\t|                         | `{:php/arr h}`          |                          |\\n432\\t+-------------------------+-------------------------+--------------------------+\\n433\\t| reference               | cell `{:php/type :ref   | exactly                  |\\n434\\t|                         | :rc n :value x :sources | `zend_reference`;        |\\n435\\t|                         | #{[o p]}}`, held        | `:sources` are the       |\\n436\\t|                         | through a marker        | typed-property type      |\\n437\\t|                         | `{:php/ref c}`          | sources (rows 41 to 47)  |\\n438\\t+-------------------------+-------------------------+--------------------------+\\n439\\t| object                  | cell `{:php/type :obj   | destruction releases     |\"}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_Zgke6ofqHDHsC1w1lnKPhOnE\",\"content\":\"640\\t|    |                                    | declares its by-reference          |\\n641\\t|    |                                    | positions in the prelude table     |\\n642\\t|    |                                    | (corner C6)                        |\\n643\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n644\\t\\n645\\t#### 4.4.2 Calls, arguments and temporaries\\n646\\t\\n647\\tZend distinguishes **borrowed** operands, which a copy `ADDREF`s, from **owned\\n648\\ttemporaries** (`TMP_VAR`), which transfer by move and are released by `FREE`\\n649\\twhen discarded or by live-temporary cleanup when an exception abandons a\\n650\\tframe. The lowering classifies each expression syntactically. Borrowed:\\n651\\tvariable, property, dimension and static-property reads, constants, literal\\n652\\tscalars. Owned: a call result, `new`, `clone`, an array literal with any\\n653\\tnon-literal element, `(array)` and `(object)` casts, a `yield` result, closure\\n654\\tcreation, the value of an assignment expression (borrowed, then `ADDREF`ed),\\n655\\tand `match` or ternary results when the chosen arm is owned (registered at the\\n656\\tarm). String interpolation produces plain uncounted values.\\n657\\t\\n658\\tA **pending call** is an owned record on the activation's temp list, created\\n659\\twhen the call expression begins and consumed when the callee is entered.\\n660\\t\\n661\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n662\\t| #  | Construct (handler)                | Rule                               |\\n663\\t+====+====================================+====================================+\\n664\\t| 13 | by-value parameter                 | row 33 or 34 at evaluation, moved  |\\n665\\t|    | (`SEND_VAR`/`SEND_VAL`, `RECV`)    | into the callee's slot at entry    |\\n666\\t|    |                                    | (row 58)                           |\\n667\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n668\\t| 14 | by-reference parameter             | row 35 at evaluation               |\\n669\\t|    | (`SEND_REF`, `RECV`)               |                                    |\\n670\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n671\\t| 15 | `return` (`RETURN`)                | row 36                             |\\n672\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n673\\t| 16 | function exit, normal or unwinding | `RELEASE_CVS`: the lowering wraps  |\\n674\\t|    | (`zend_free_compiled_variables`)   | every body that declares locals or |\\n675\\t|    |                                    | parameters in `php/try-finally`    |\\n676\\t|    |                                    | with `php/release-cvs`             |\\n677\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n678\\t| 32 | owned temporary produced           | `php/tmp! v`: a counted `v` is     |\\n679\\t|    |                                    | pushed on the activation's temp    |\\n680\\t|    |                                    | list and returned; uncounted       |\\n681\\t|    |                                    | values are not registered (the     |\\n682\\t|    |                                    | producing operation already holds  |\\n683\\t|    |                                    | the count)                         |\\n684\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n685\\t| 33 | argument from a borrowed operand   | immediately `ADDREF` and append to |\\n686\\t|    | (`SEND_VAR`)                       | the pending call's `:args`, before |\\n687\\t|    |                                    | the next argument expression runs  |\\n688\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n689\\t| 34 | argument from an owned temporary   | immediately move: unregister from  |\\n690\\t|    | (`SEND_VAL`)                       | the temp list and append to        |\\n691\\t|    |                                    | `:args`                            |\\n692\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n693\\t| 35 | by-reference argument (`SEND_REF`) | immediately rows 4 or 5 (write     |\\n694\\t|    |                                    | fetch, `MAKE_REF`, `ADDREF`) into  |\\n695\\t|    |                                    | `:args`; a non-variable operand    |\\n696\\t|    |                                    | for a by-reference parameter is    |\\n697\\t|    |                                    | `Notice: Only variables should be  |\\n698\\t|    |                                    | passed by reference` and a         |\\n699\\t|    |                                    | by-value send, decided now (the    |\\n700\\t|    |                                    | oracle pins the prefer-ref         |\\n701\\t|    |                                    | builtins)                          |\\n702\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n703\\t| 36 | return into the caller (`RETURN`)  | borrowed: `ADDREF`; owned: move;   |\\n704\\t|    |                                    | the value becomes the caller's     |\\n705\\t|    |                                    | owned temporary (`php/tmp!` at the |\\n706\\t|    |                                    | call site); then row 16 releases   |\\n707\\t|    |                                    | the callee's CVs (the moved        |\\n708\\t|    |                                    | parameters balance) and every      |\\n709\\t|    |                                    | temporary still on the callee's    |\\n710\\t|    |                                    | list                               |\\n711\\t+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\n712\\t| 37 | expression statement with a        | at statement end `php/release-tmps |\\n713\\t|    | discarded result (`FREE`)          | mark` releases every temporary     |\\n714\\t|    |                                    | registered since the statement's   |\\n715\\t|    |                                    | mar