 live-after-collection\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:119:(defn- changing-caller-source\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:132:(deftest ^:slow reachable-heap-is-stable-under-delegation-test\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:135:      (let [small (live-after-collection k (changing-caller-source 10))\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:136:            large (live-after-collection k (changing-caller-source 1000))]\"}\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_lT20OSARruxXAukgGgd9EAUR\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj\\\",\\\"line_offset\\\":1210,\\\"n_lines\\\":90}\"}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_Dhy3TdSucP9fqhc6riFDoiLw\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"docs/design/yang.antlr.md\\\",\\\"line_offset\\\":1940,\\\"n_lines\\\":70}\"}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_rPdsl4iKkDlp7W5jwOBId93S\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\\\",\\\"line_offset\\\":2470,\\\"n_lines\\\":135}\"}}]}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_Dhy3TdSucP9fqhc6riFDoiLw\",\"content\":\"1940\\toptimization belongs to an attached optimizer and must preserve these\\n1941\\tobservations and runtime rebinding of the consumer. List, set, and dict\\n1942\\tcomprehensions stay eager. `yield` at module or class level, or inside\\n1943\\tany comprehension or generator expression, is a syntax diagnostic.\\n1944\\t\\n1945\\t`py/iter-at` keeps its index signature as an internal compatibility\\n1946\\tinterface, not the public iterator protocol (ruling 5). A stateful\\n1947\\titerator advances once per call and ignores the index; iterable\\n1948\\tacquisition happens once per loop; `iter(iterator)` preserves identity;\\n1949\\texhaustion handling covers only the advancement, never the loop body.\\n1950\\tThe loop counter must not overflow or round under long consumption: it\\n1951\\tuses exact increment once C3 lands, without narrowing generator\\n1952\\tpayloads.\\n1953\\t\\n1954\\tUser-defined iterator classes are part of C2, in S5 (ruling 8).\\n1955\\tImplicit `__iter__` and `__next__` lookup uses the type's special-method\\n1956\\tpath, since ordinary `py/getattr` prefers instance attributes; it\\n1957\\tvalidates the returned iterator and catches `StopIteration` only around\\n1958\\tadvancement. Termination values are preserved for delegation, other\\n1959\\texceptions propagate, and optional `send`, `throw`, and `close` are\\n1960\\tforwarded per PEP 380.\\n1961\\t\\n1962\\tNo generator flag is persisted on function specs (ruling 9). Generator\\n1963\\tstatus is decided during scope-aware lowering, excluding nested function\\n1964\\tbodies and including unreachable `yield` and `yield from`, and is\\n1965\\tencoded in ordinary code. Future introspection, such as\\n1966\\t`inspect.isgeneratorfunction`, derives status from the scoped\\n1967\\tgenerator-construction pattern; a query for direct applications of\\n1968\\t`py/yield` alone is insufficient, because a body using only `yield from`\\n1969\\tneed not apply it.\\n1970\\t\\n1971\\tHeap, identity, and wire:\\n1972\\t\\n1973\\t- Tracing needs no VM change: cell content is traced as data and a\\n1974\\t  continuation is walked through its payload.\\n1975\\t- An unreachable generator is reclaimed without an implicit `close()`\\n1976\\t  (ruling 6). Python specifies a `close()` on generator finalization, so\\n1977\\t  this is an explicit finalization restriction of the support profile,\\n1978\\t  not conformance. The landed collector has no finalizers; explicit\\n1979\\t  `close()` stays supported. Pinning roots the generator cell and traces\\n1980\\t  its current content, not every historical continuation.\\n1981\\t- `%capture` is undelimited, so `:resume` holds the frames of the first\\n1982\\t  `next()` call beneath the generator's own (stale base). This fixed\\n1983\\t  retention is accepted for C2; growth per yield is rejected (ruling 7).\\n1984\\t  Delimited capture is a separate VM question.\\n1985\\t- A suspended generator does not migrate: cells refuse lift and\\n1986\\t  continuations refuse as `:non-canonicalizable`. Once heap lift and a\\n1987\\t  continuation encoding land, generators migrate with no\\n1988\\t  generator-specific wire form; until then the refusal stays.\\n1989\\t- `is` is `=` on the ref, `iter(g) is g`, and a generator is a dict key\\n1990\\t  by ref through the non-numeric arm of `py/key`. `py/snapshot-obj`\\n1991\\t  renders `{:py/generator name}`, diagnostic data, never a resumable\\n1992\\t  wire form. The prelude compares only `:state` keywords, never\\n1993\\t  generator contents, since continuation equality and hash are\\n1994\\t  structural.\\n1995\\t- The canonical tree changes only by new prelude functions: `yield` is\\n1996\\t  an `:application` of `py/yield`, and `%capture` stays inside the\\n1997\\t  prelude. The prelude grows, so every bundled unit's address changes,\\n1998\\t  a prelude-profile bump under section 11.\\n1999\\t\\n2000\\tFor safepoints, generator switches happen only at applications of\\n2001\\t`py/gen-switch`, `py/yield-raw`, and `py/yield-from`, which an attached\\n2002\\tinserter can find by query; `sys.settrace` sees nothing in C2. Future\\n2003\\tper-thread dynamic state (the frame-record stack, the recursion counter,\\n2004\\t`exc_info`) joins `:ctx` and swaps with the handler stack.\\n2005\\t\\n2006\\t```text\\n2007\\t+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n2008\\t| Slice  | Scope                                                               |\\n2009\\t+========+=====================================================================+\"}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_rPdsl4iKkDlp7W5jwOBId93S\",\"content\":\"2470\\t    (let [id (:id x)\\n2471\\t          entry (get heap id)]\\n2472\\t      (when (and (some? entry) (= (:seal x) (:seal entry))) id))))\\n2473\\t\\n2474\\t\\n2475\\t(defn- moded\\n2476\\t  \\\"`work` with each of `xs` pushed in `mode`, `:kernel` or `:data`.\\\"\\n2477\\t  [work mode xs]\\n2478\\t  (into work (map (fn [x] [mode x])) xs))\\n2479\\t\\n2480\\t\\n2481\\t(defn- trace\\n2482\\t  \\\"`found` plus the ids of `heap` reachable from `roots`, a map\\n2483\\t   `{:kernel [...] :data [...]}` of root values by mode. Two modes keep\\n2484\\t   guest data from being read as kernel shapes (gemini reclamation gate,\\n2485\\t   concern 1):\\n2486\\t\\n2487\\t   - `:kernel`, a value in a kernel position (a kernel root, an engine\\n2488\\t     table entry, a closure or continuation payload, or a kernel child of\\n2489\\t     one): the kernel's `gc-children` may interpret it, and answers which\\n2490\\t     of its children are kernel positions and which are values. A value\\n2491\\t     it does not recognize is walked whole, as data.\\n2492\\t   - `:data`, a value position (an environment value, an operand, a\\n2493\\t     register, a cell's content): every map is walked whole, never\\n2494\\t     pruned, so a guest map shaped like a frame cannot hide a cell ref.\\n2495\\t     Only a closure or continuation, a host type no guest can forge,\\n2496\\t     re-enters `:kernel` mode through its payload.\\n2497\\t\\n2498\\t   Scalars hold nothing. With `follow?` a newly found id's content is\\n2499\\t   traced too, as data (marking); without, only the refs met directly\\n2500\\t   (pinning). Each value is visited once per mode, so shared environments\\n2501\\t   cost one walk and a cell holding its own ref terminates. The worklist\\n2502\\t   is explicit: a deep continuation chain does not grow the host stack.\\\"\\n2503\\t  [vm heap roots found follow?]\\n2504\\t  (let [children-of (if (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\\n2505\\t                      #(module/gc-children vm %)\\n2506\\t                      (constantly nil))]\\n2507\\t    (loop [work (-> ()\\n2508\\t                    (moded :kernel (:kernel roots))\\n2509\\t                    (moded :data (:data roots)))\\n2510\\t           seen #{}\\n2511\\t           found found]\\n2512\\t      (if (empty? work)\\n2513\\t        found\\n2514\\t        (let [[mode x :as entry] (peek work)\\n2515\\t              work (pop work)]\\n2516\\t          (if (or (scalar? x) (contains? seen entry))\\n2517\\t            (recur work seen found)\\n2518\\t            (let [id (when (map? x) (heap-ref-id heap x))\\n2519\\t                  new-id? (and (some? id) (not (contains? found id)))\\n2520\\t                  children (when (and (= :kernel mode)\\n2521\\t                                      (not (values/host-typed? x)))\\n2522\\t                             (children-of x))\\n2523\\t                  work (cond-> work\\n2524\\t                         (and new-id? follow?)\\n2525\\t                         (conj [:data (:value (get heap id))])\\n2526\\t                         (values/host-typed? x)\\n2527\\t                         (conj [:kernel (values/payload x)])\\n2528\\t                         (some? children)\\n2529\\t                         (-> (moded :kernel (:kernel children))\\n2530\\t                             (moded :data (:values children)))\\n2531\\t                         (and (nil? children) (map? x))\\n2532\\t                         (-> (moded :data (keys x))\\n2533\\t                             (moded :data (vals x)))\\n2534\\t                         (and (nil? children) (not (map? x)) (coll? x))\\n2535\\t                         (moded :data x))]\\n2536\\t              (recur work\\n2537\\t                     (conj seen entry)\\n2538\\t                     (if new-id? (conj found id) found)))))))))\\n2539\\t\\n2540\\t\\n2541\\t(defn- gc-roots\\n2542\\t  \\\"Every root of `vm` (design Q1), by mode: the kernel's registers as it\\n2543\\t   classifies them (`module/gc-roots`), each entry of `:parked`,\\n2544\\t   `:wait-set` and `:ready-queue` as a kernel position, the store and\\n2545\\t   every module store as values, then `extra` as values. Code, images,\\n2546\\t   the registry, primitives, `:callable-effects`, telemetry and\\n2547\\t   `:resources` are not roots: a literal can never be an authentic ref,\\n2548\\t   and a value inside a stream is the medium's (hence pinning).\\\"\\n2549\\t  [vm extra]\\n2550\\t  (let [kernel (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\\n2551\\t                 (module/gc-roots vm))]\\n2552\\t    {:kernel (-> (vec (:kernel kernel))\\n2553\\t                 (into (vals (:parked vm)))\\n2554\\t                 (into (:wait-set vm))\\n2555\\t                 (into (:ready-queue vm))),\\n2556\\t     :data (-> [(:store vm) (:module-stores vm)]\\n2557\\t               (into (:values kernel))\\n2558\\t               (into extra))}))\\n2559\\t\\n2560\\t\\n2561\\t(defn- mark\\n2562\\t  \\\"The ids of `heap` live from `roots` and from the `pinned` ids: a pinned\\n2563\\t   cell is a root, so its content is traced too, as data.\\\"\\n2564\\t  [vm heap roots pinned]\\n2565\\t  (let [pins (filterv #(contains? heap %) pinned)]\\n2566\\t    (trace vm\\n2567\\t           heap\\n2568\\t           (update roots :data into (map #(:value (get heap %))) pins)\\n2569\\t           (set pins)\\n2570\\t           true)))\\n2571\\t\\n2572\\t\\n2573\\t(defn- sweep\\n2574\\t  \\\"`heap` without each id of the cycle's `snapshot` that `marked` lacks.\\n2575\\t   An id allocated after the snapshot is not in it, so it is spared.\\\"\\n2576\\t  [heap snapshot marked]\\n2577\\t  (reduce-kv (fn [h id _] (if (contains? marked id) h (dissoc h id)))\\n2578\\t             heap\\n2579\\t             snapshot))\\n2580\\t\\n2581\\t\\n2582\\t(defn- gc-of\\n2583\\t  [state]\\n2584\\t  (or (:gc state) (vm/fresh-gc nil)))\\n2585\\t\\n2586\\t\\n2587\\t(defn collect\\n2588\\t  \\\"`vm` after one stop-the-world collection of its `:heap`, with `extra`\\n2589\\t   traced as additional roots. The allocation count restarts and the\\n2590\\t   threshold becomes `max(base, 2 x live)`, so the total work stays linear\\n2591\\t   in allocations. Pure: the same state always collects to the same heap.\\\"\\n2592\\t  ([vm] (collect vm nil))\\n2593\\t  ([vm extra]\\n2594\\t   (let [gc (gc-of vm)\\n2595\\t         snapshot (:heap vm)\\n2596\\t         marked (mark vm snapshot (gc-roots vm extra) (:pinned gc))\\n2597\\t         heap (sweep (:heap vm) snapshot marked)]\\n2598\\t     (assoc vm\\n2599\\t            :heap heap\\n2600\\t            :gc (assoc gc\\n2601\\t                       :since 0\\n2602\\t                       :threshold (max (:base gc) (* 2 (count heap))))))))\\n2603\\t\\n2604\\t\"}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_lT20OSARruxXAukgGgd9EAUR\",\"content\":\"1210\\t            generator's :resume grows per item\\\"\\n1211\\t    (doseq [k [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register]]\\n1212\\t      (testing (str k)\\n1213\\t        (is (= (suspended-resume-sizes k 2 (counter-source 10 true))\\n1214\\t               (suspended-resume-sizes k 2 (counter-source 1000 true))))))))\\n1215\\t\\n1216\\t\\n1217\\t(defn- deep-size\\n1218\\t  \\\"Node count of `x` with continuation and closure payloads followed; a\\n1219\\t   cell ref counts as itself (its cell is counted once, as a heap entry).\\\"\\n1220\\t  [x]\\n1221\\t  (cond\\n1222\\t    (values/host-typed? x) (+ 1 (deep-size (values/payload x)))\\n1223\\t    (map? x) (reduce + 1 (map deep-size (concat (keys x) (vals x))))\\n1224\\t    (coll? x) (reduce + 1 (map deep-size x))\\n1225\\t    :else 1))\\n1226\\t\\n1227\\t\\n1228\\t(defn- live-after-collection\\n1229\\t  \\\"[live cell count, deep size of all live cell content] once VM `k` ran\\n1230\\t   `source` and its final state was collected with the suspended\\n1231\\t   generator named `root` as the only extra root: everything that\\n1232\\t   generator reaches, continuations followed, not one `:resume` alone.\\n1233\\t   The module's own globals are garbage once it completes, so without the\\n1234\\t   root nothing of the program would be live.\\\"\\n1235\\t  [k source root]\\n1236\\t  (let [ast (lower/lower-packet\\n1237\\t              (parser/parse-source (parser/make-worker) [:u 1] source))\\n1238\\t        final ((get final-vms k) ast (vm/ast->datoms ast))\\n1239\\t        roots (into []\\n1240\\t                    (keep (fn [[id {:keys [value seal]}]]\\n1241\\t                            (when (and (= :generator (:py/type value))\\n1242\\t                                       (= :suspended (:state value))\\n1243\\t                                       (= root (:name value)))\\n1244\\t                              {:type :cell-ref, :id id, :seal seal})))\\n1245\\t                    (:heap final))\\n1246\\t        heap (:heap (engine/collect final roots))]\\n1247\\t    (is (= 1 (count roots)) (str k \\\" one suspended \\\" root))\\n1248\\t    [(count heap) (reduce + (map (fn [[_ {:keys [value]}]] (deep-size value)) heap))]))\\n1249\\t\\n1250\\t\\n1251\\t(defn- changing-caller-source\\n1252\\t  \\\"`n` items through a `yield from` level, resumed alternately by a\\n1253\\t   function and by a fresh generator dropped after one step.\\\"\\n1254\\t  [n]\\n1255\\t  (lines \\\"def g():\\\"\\n1256\\t         \\\"    i = 0\\\"\\n1257\\t         \\\"    while True:\\\"\\n1258\\t         \\\"        yield i\\\"\\n1259\\t         \\\"        i += 1\\\"\\n1260\\t         \\\"def h():\\\"\\n1261\\t         \\\"    yield from g()\\\"\\n1262\\t         \\\"it = h()\\\"\\n1263\\t         \\\"def by_function(x):\\\"\\n1264\\t         \\\"    return next(x)\\\"\\n1265\\t         \\\"def by_generator(x):\\\"\\n1266\\t         \\\"    yield next(x)\\\"\\n1267\\t         \\\"k = 0\\\"\\n1268\\t         (str \\\"while k < \\\" n \\\":\\\")\\n1269\\t         \\\"    if k % 2 == 0:\\\"\\n1270\\t         \\\"        by_function(it)\\\"\\n1271\\t         \\\"    else:\\\"\\n1272\\t         \\\"        next(by_generator(it))\\\"\\n1273\\t         \\\"    k += 1\\\"))\\n1274\\t\\n1275\\t\\n1276\\t(deftest ^:slow reachable-heap-is-stable-under-delegation-test\\n1277\\t  (testing \\\"after a forced collection, the live heap (cells and their content,\\n1278\\t            continuations followed) is the same after 10 and after 1000 items\\n1279\\t            resumed through yield from by changing callers: no retention\\n1280\\t            grows per item or per caller\\\"\\n1281\\t    (doseq [k [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register]]\\n1282\\t      (testing (str k)\\n1283\\t        (is (= (live-after-collection k (changing-caller-source 10) \\\"h\\\")\\n1284\\t               (live-after-collection k (changing-caller-source 1000) \\\"h\\\")))))))\\n1285\\t\\n1286\\t\\n1287\\t;; =============================================================================\\n1288\\t;; S5 acceptance: user-defined iterators, snapshot rendering, dropped generators\\n1289\\t;; =============================================================================\\n1290\\t\\n1291\\t(deftest user-iterator-class-test\\n1292\\t  (testing \\\"a class with __iter__ and __next__ drives for, list, next and\\n1293\\t            unpacking; a shared iterator keeps its position across loops\\\"\\n1294\\t    (every-vm= (prints \\\"[3, 4, 5]\\\" \\\"done\\\" \\\"[1, 2, 3]\\\" \\\"1 2\\\")\\n1295\\t               (lines \\\"class Count:\\\"\\n1296\\t                      \\\"    def __init__(self, n):\\\"\\n1297\\t                      \\\"        self.i = 0\\\"\\n1298\\t                      \\\"        self.n = n\\\"\\n1299\\t                      \\\"    def __iter__(self):\\\"\"}\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"## Ruling: **(c), the measurement is wrong—not the assertion**\\n\\nThe PHP fixture blocks **before module shutdown**. Consequently, `engine/collect` still traces the blocked main activation, its globals, continuation, and temporary/CV state in addition to the supplied generator reference. The `roots` argument contains **extra roots**, not replacement roots (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2541-2558`, `:2587-2597`).\\n\\nThus 151 versus 5,596 cells measures different module-frame live sets, not growth owned by the suspended generator. There is no evidence here of a generator retention leak.\\n\\nThe last `$j` is not the essential problem: the blocker is after the caller loop, so its statement cleanup should already have run. The decisive error is comparing heaps while the entire caller/module activation remains live.\\n\\n### Required correction\\n\\nPort the Python fixture’s measurement protocol (`test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:1228-1248`):\\n\\n1. Run the PHP program **to normal completion**, without injecting the blocker.\\n2. Preserve the suspended `h` through its deliberate `$it->self = $it` cycle.\\n3. Locate that one suspended generator in the final heap.\\n4. Call `engine/collect` with it as an extra root.\\n5. Assert equality of both cell count and deep content size at N=10 and N=1000.\\n\\nAfter normal module exit, PHP’s CV and temporary cleanup must remove the caller’s ownership (`docs/design/yang.php.md:399-401`, `:673-676`, `:712-738`), leaving the cycle-rooted generator and its genuinely live delegation state. This is the same isolation strategy already used by the passing Python test.\\n\\n### Generator semantics relied upon\\n\\n- A suspended generator legitimately retains its current frame, CVs, continuation, current/key, and delegate. Neither `$i` incrementing nor repeated `yield from` requires retaining every historical yield or caller.\\n- `%capture` may retain a fixed stale base; **growth per yield is explicitly rejected** by ruling 7 (`docs/design/yang.antlr.md:1971-1984`).\\n- Generator destruction releases CVs without running pending `finally` blocks; that does not justify per-iteration retention (`docs/design/yang.php.md:341-348`).\\n- Tracing follows continuation and closure payloads, so the existing deep-size measurement is appropriate.\\n\\n**Engineer round:** change only `live-after-collection` to use a final VM state, as Python does. Keep the N=10/N=1000 equality assertion unchanged. Do not change the generator runtime or cleanup code on the basis of this failing fixture. If the corrected fixture still grows, that result—not the current one—would justify a runtime leak investigation.\"}\n{\"role\":\"meta\",\"type\":\"session.resume_hint\",\"session_id\":\"session_858c39c2-7881-4a2b-b649-c6707fe0c4ce\",\"command\":\"kimi -r session_858c39c2-7881-4a2b-b649-c6707fe0c4ce\",\"content\":\"To resume this session: kimi -r session_858c39c2-7881-4a2b-b649-c6707fe0c4ce\"}\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:129:(defn run-raw\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:36:    (is (= \"01\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:39:    (is (= \"23\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:42:    (is (= \"aabc\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:45:    (is (= \"43s\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:60:(def ^:private final-vms\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:73:(defn- deep-size\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:105:        blocked ((get final-vms k) ast (vm/ast->datoms ast))]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:109:                                (when (and (= \"h\" (get-in value [:gen :name]))\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:110:                                           (= :suspended (get-in value [:gen :state])))\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:114:          (let [heap (:heap (engine/collect blocked roots))]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:116:             (deep-size (mapv :value (vals heap)))]))))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3721:           (if (not (nil? (get (php/obj-state o) :gen)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3994:           (if (nil? (get (php/obj-state o) :gen))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4277:    [php/gen-state (fn [g] (get (php/obj-state g) :gen))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/